Subject: [PATCH] refactor: separate timestamps from lyrics (Option B for
 500-song scalability)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DESIGN DECISION: Lyrics text stays CLEAN (no timestamps). Timing stored
separately in chordChart.slides[]. This scales to 500+ songs because
re-analysis regenerates timing without corrupting lyrics.

sections[].text = '[B]The Lord bless you [E]and keep you\n...'  ← CLEAN
chordChart.slides[] = [{startMs: 17937, endMs: 32500, ...}]     ← TIMING

Changes:
- REMOVED: {M:SS.mmm} timestamp bracket system from text
- REMOVED: RecalculateSlideTimingFromText (was inserting timestamps into text)
- REMOVED: {timestamp} stripping from ChordChartWindow display
- REMOVED: SlideTimestampRegex, ExtractSlideBlocks, SetSlideTimestamps,
  ParseTimecodeToMs, StripChordsAndTimestamps from being used for text modification

- ADDED: RecalculateSlideTimings() - simple, clean version that:
  1. Counts slide blocks (empty lines in text)
  2. Divides section time EVENLY by slide count
  3. Stores timing in chordChart.slides[] (separate from text)
  4. Generates MIDI cues for Presenter auto-advance
  5. Runs automatically on Save in sub-section editor

- KEPT: ChordProParserService utility methods (still useful for parsing)
- KEPT: chordChart.slides[].ManualTiming flag (for future manual timing UI)

Benefits for 500-song database:
- Re-analyze any song → timing regenerates, lyrics untouched
- Bulk operations safe (never corrupt text)
- Lyrics are always YOUR exact pasted text
- Timing is always derivable from section boundaries
